;tmux stands for terminal multiplexer and it is used in managing terminals inside of terminals

;its package is usually tmux

;to open it type: tmux , in the terminal

;the default prefix is ^B

;to detach, meaning to get out of a session without closing it:
prefix + D

;to reattach to the most recent session type: tmux attach

;tmux can create horizontal and vertical splits, called panes

;to make a vertical split (make a pane on the right):
prefix + % (by default)

;to make a horizontal split (make a pane downwards):
prefix + " (by default)

;to exit tmux exit the last terminal open in a session

;to see currently running tmux sessions use:
tmux list-sessions
;to exit a pane in tmux is prefix + X + y (by default)

;to create a  new window in tmux:
tmux new-window
OR: prefix + C (by default)

;to move between windows:
prefix + P for previous
prefix + N for next
(by default)

;to kill a window:
prefix + & (by default)

;to rename a window, while on it:
prefix + , (by default)

